# Repo-level wiring gate: modules under app/ with no static importer outside
# themselves and the test tree.
#
# Two rules, both enforced by tests/test_module_wiring.py:
#   1. Every entry needs a reason after the '#'.
#   2. An entry deferring to future wiring must say what would expire it, and
#      it is a FAILURE to leave the entry in place once that has happened.
#
# Gate 4 (tests/trigger_engine/test_wiring.py) checks wiring *within* a module.
# It cannot see a module that nothing imports at all — its scope boundary is
# exactly where that defect lives. This is the companion check.

middlewares    # config-loaded extension point: `use: app.middlewares.truncation:...` in config.yaml, no static importer by design
tools          # config-loaded extension point: `use: app.tools.openclaude:openclaude_coder` in config.yaml, same
